From: Douglas Teles <dga.teles@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3326: keep a crashed boot's log, reset a hung one

Users report consoles that freeze at random (in a game, in a menu, while
booting) and stay black until the reset button, and those boots leave
nothing behind: the journal is volatile and no ramoops region exists,
though the kernel has PSTORE_RAM and userspace already reports what
/sys/fs/pstore keeps.

Reserve 1 MiB for ramoops at 0x1f000000, inside the RAM of every RK3326
board (the smallest show ~730 MiB), with room for the console log and
oops records, and enable the SoC watchdog so userspace (systemd's
RuntimeWatchdogSec) can reset a console that stops answering.

Signed-off-by: Douglas Teles <dga.teles@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326.dtsi
@@ -6,6 +6,26 @@
 
 #include "px30.dtsi"
 
+/ {
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+
+		ramoops@1f000000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x0 0x1f000000 0x0 0x100000>;
+			record-size = <0x20000>;
+			console-size = <0x80000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x20000>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&wdt {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &display_subsystem {
 	ports = <&vopb_out>;
 };
